<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-RTZ-CRA sees $1.5 bln capex.</title>
<headline>RTRS-RTZ-CRA sees $1.5 bln capex.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>RTZ Corp Plc-CRA Ltd will spend some US$1.5 billion annually over the next few years on capital expenditure, executive chairman Robert Wilson said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;What we're looking at is in the order of around $1.5 billion in the next three or four years,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>Wilson also said that the group's gearing ratio of 22 percent was low.</p>
<p>&quot;We are currently at 22 percent debt to debt-plus-equity which we will certainly acknowledge is a comparatively low level of gearing,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>&quot;But over the years the figures have shot up and down through very considerable expense in this group, with a huge range,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne bureau 61-3 9286 1421</p>
</text>
